Description: CVE-2026-40393 - Use STACK_ARRAY instead of NIR_VLA
 The number of struct fields (SPIR-V OpTypeStruct / vtn_type_get_nir_type)
 and the number of call parameters (NIR function inlining) are controlled by
 an untrusted shader, so using alloca() via NIR_VLA can overflow the stack
 and lead to out-of-bounds memory access. Replace NIR_VLA with STACK_ARRAY,
 which falls back to malloc() for large sizes, and release it with
 STACK_ARRAY_FINISH on every exit path. Adds the util/stack_array.h helper,
 which is not present in mesa 20.3.5.
 .
 Backport of upstream commits 978fd42b (spirv) and 45ce75f3 (nir), adapted
 to 20.3.5 (nir_ssa_def, nir_inline_functions.c).
Origin: upstream, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/commit/978fd42b4b7d1e9c0435ffa7e1a4d339cba9b76e
Bug: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-40393
Author: Root.io Security <security@root.io>
Last-Update: 2026-10-06
